  "query_preview": "(Labor Day through Thursday)...\nHigher surf will continue into Labor Day, then slowly subside \ninto Tuesday and Wednesday. Mid and higher level tropical \nmoisture will be decreasing on Labor Day into Tuesday. \n\nWarmer nights will continue into early next week with warmer high\ntemperatures for Labor Day through Wednesday as drying occurs. \nHigh temperatures for next Wednesday will be within a few degrees \nof average for the mountains and deserts and a few to around 5 \ndegrees above average for the coast and valleys. \n\nHigh temperatures for next Wednesday will range from around 80 \nnear the coast to the 90s for the Inland Empire with the lower \ndeserts around 105. Low temperatures will be mostly in the mid 60s\nto lower 70s for the coast and valleys and in the mid 70s to mid \n80s for the lower deserts.",
